{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794353007000-engineer-cc2-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1210,1340p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1750,1835p'\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-10 23:30:45 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 06:30:45 +07\n\n# cc2 fix round r4 — recorder evidence and wrapper provenance (astra re-confirm residue)\n\nWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2`, branch `cc2-transform-session-c1` @ `2d170926` + uncommitted r3 changes, left dirty, NOTHING committed. Bounds respected: r4 edits only three of the six permitted files (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`, `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`); the r3 change to `src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc` is untouched by r4. `vm/macro.cljc`, `vm/semantic/*`, `yang/clojure.cljc`, `core/prelude.cljc`, `vm/linker/dht.cljc`, `vm.cljc`, and `yin/repl/index.cljc` untouched — no fix required them (the commit evidence is captured in `yin.repl` from the indexer's before/after state and published-manifest snapshots, per the indexer's own `step`/`publish` contract at `index.cljc:419-487`). Origins never minted; canonical bytes unchanged; legacy paths byte-identical; fail-closed everywhere.\n\nNOTE (placement): this session's sandbox permits writes only under the cc2 worktree, so this file was written to the worktree's own `collab/yang-clojure/` mirror of the deliverable path `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794353007000-engineer-cc2-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md`. The orchestrator can move it verbatim; no prior findings file was touched either way.\n\n## Per-finding disposition\n\n### 1. F2 residue — the recorder pairs from COMMIT EVIDENCE, not index search\n\nFixed. `record-call-site-admissions` no longer searches all unmapped programs in the published index.\n\n- [src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1790](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1790) (`eval-program`): before the index stage runs, the round captures its commit evidence — `{:programs-before (indexed-program-roots (:indexer expanded)) :indexer-before (:indexer expanded)}` — and attaches it as the transient `:call-site-commit-evidence` (line 1803) for the recorder, which consumes and dissocs it (line 1290-1291). Recording is no longer gated on `forwarded` alone.\n- [src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1255](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1255): `index-round-succeeded?` verifies the indexing/publication SUCCEEDED — no recorded `:failure`, not `:lost?`, a manifest present, `:published` covering every `:transactions`, and at least one new transaction. This is exactly the evidence `yin.repl.index/publish` (index.cljc:419-450) leaves: a failed commit or publication preserves the prior manifest and records `:failure`, so such a round proves nothing and records nothing. Partial failures are all-or-nothing at this gate: any recorded failure refuses every pairing of the round (claim-free), even for packets that did commit.\n- [src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1270](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1270): `record-call-site-admissions` pairs only programs ABSENT from `:programs-before` — the entities the current round's successful commit actually committed. Pre-existing indexed entities, including rehydrated programs, are excluded by construction, so a new admission can never be assigned to an old unmapped program. Absent/unreadable evidence (`nil` programs-before/after, missing evidence) records nothing.\n- Uniqueness on BOTH sides (lines 1308-1322): new entries and newly committed candidates are grouped by root; a root pairs only when it has exactly one new admission AND exactly one newly committed candidate AND that candidate is not already mapped. Multiple admissions or multiple candidates for one root refuse all of them (unmapped, claim-free publication) — never first-wins. No counter is read or compared anywhere.\n- [src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1238](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1238): `indexed-program-roots` now answers `[]` (not nil) when nothing is published yet, keeping \"empty index\" distinct from \"unreadable index\" (nil, fail-closed).\n- Rehydration behaviour, stated explicitly (docstring at [repl.cljc:1217](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1217), session init at line 788): the mapping starts empty on a fresh session (`:call-site-admissions {}` in `make-session`) and is NOT reconstructed across rehydration — `create-state` rehydrates only the indexer (line ~970), and `rebuild-session` merges a fresh `make-session`, so the mapping resets while the durable index carries over. Claim-free recovery for rehydrated sessions is the accepted policy; no reconstruction was invented.\n\n### 2. F6 — wrapper provenance from retained assembly evidence\n\nFixed. Plumbing did not require forbidden files, so no STOP was needed.\n\n- [src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:905](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:905) (`module-from-index`): assembly retains its computed wrapper set (the `sequenced-wrapper-paths` set it already computed at ~:843) on the spec it hands forward as `:call-site-wrappers-evidence`, beside the existing `:call-site-wrappers`.\n- [src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:636](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:636): `recovered-call-site-claim` now takes the retained evidence (wired at lines 290-295, `::absent` sentinel when the spec carries none) and, whenever recovered rows are claimed, requires the spec's `:call-site-wrappers` set to EQUAL that evidence — same set, no duplicates on either side (lines 673-683). Any divergence refuses as `{:wrapper-provenance {:expected ... :actual ...}}`, surfaced by `publish-closure!` (lines 317-318) as `:yin.link.publish/wrapper-provenance`. A caller-supplied wrapper set that assembly did not compute — including one with no retained evidence at all — is never accepted. Moving a recovered user occurrence into `:call-site-wrappers` now diverges from the retained evidence and refuses instead of reassigning that call to the publication origin.\n- Unchanged degenerate path: empty/nil `:call-site-rows` still makes no claim at all (nil claim, claim-free publication), regardless of wrapper fields.\n\n### 3. F5 — the four regression cases\n\nFixed. New tests in [test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc2/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1861), each with a positive refusal/absence signal (an assertion on the empty mapping / claim-free spec / refusal reason, not merely a missing row):\n\n- (r4-1, line 1883) stale published snapshot after a failed index round: recorder records `{}` and the admission publishes claim-free via `module-from-index`.\n- (r4-2, line 1912) multiple new admissions competing for one newly committed candidate: both refuse (`{}`); (r4-2b, line 1922) multiple newly committed candidates for one admission likewise refuse — both-sides uniqueness.\n- (r4-3, line 1897) rehydrated unmapped program + new admission of the same root: no pairing (`{}`), claim-free publication.\n- (r4-4, line 1948) a recovered user occurrence moved into `:call-site-wrappers`: publication REFUSED with reason `:yin.link.publish/wrapper-provenance`; (r4-4b, line 1960) a wrapper set with the retained evidence dissoc'd is likewise refused with that reason, and the valid spec is asserted to carry `:call-site-wrappers-evidence` (line 1945).\n\nRed-first evidence: with only the r4 tests added (no source fix), the suite ran **31 tests, 348 assertions, 10 failures, 0 errors** — every failure inside the new r4 cases (stale snapshot paired, rehydrated program claimed, competing admission first-won, no wrapper evidence retained, moved occurrence published under the publication origin). (r4-2b passes on the old code too — the old candidate-count check already refused that side; it is kept as coverage of the both-sides rule.) After the fix: same 348 assertions, 0 failures.\n\n## Verification (all foreground, nothing backgrounded)\n\n| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` (pre-fix, r4 tests only) | 31 tests, 348 assertions, **10 failures**, 0 errors (authentic reproduction) |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` (final) | **31 tests, 348 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.linker.publish-test -n yang.safepoint-test -n yin.repl.query-test` | **48 tests, 453 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.index-test` (recorder wiring regression) | **73 tests, 510 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test -n yin.repl.dht-test` (publish-name path) | **69 tests, 827 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** |\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n\n## Notes / unverified\n\n- The recorder's success gate treats any recorded indexer `:failure` as refusing the whole round's pairings, including a failure carried from an earlier round that this round's publication did not clear (only `:publish`/`:materialize` failures are cleared by a successful round, index.cljc:298,447). That can only cost a claim (claim-free publication), never mint a wrong one — the fail-closed direction.\n- A round whose expander forwards several packets pairs each only via the before/after entity diff; packets are committed one transaction each (index.cljc `step`), so the diff is exactly the round's committed set.\n- The kit contract test was not run (orchestrator runs it separately, per prior rounds).\n- Nothing was committed, as instructed.\n  1210\t   custody): the retained record a session publication recovers its\n  1211\t   claim from (`yin.vm.linker.publish/module-from-index`'\n  1212\t   `:call-site-tables` option). Nil before any claimed expansion.\"\n  1213\t  [state]\n  1214\t  (:call-site-tables (:expander state)))\n  1215\t\n  1216\t\n  1217\t(defn call-site-admissions\n  1218\t  \"The explicit indexed-program -> full-admission-origin mapping the\n  1219\t   session records at the point where the expander and the code indexer\n  1220\t   agree: the round in which the expander staged a program (retaining\n  1221\t   its table under `[admission-origin final-root]`) is the round in\n  1222\t   which the indexer committed that same program, so the newly indexed\n  1223\t   program's metadata entity is paired with that entry's full origin\n  1224\t   (`yin.vm.linker.publish/module-from-index`'\n  1225\t   `:call-site-admissions` option). No counter is compared: a program\n  1226\t   the round cannot pair uniquely is left unmapped, and recovery for\n  1227\t   it is refused. Empty before any claimed, indexed expansion.\n  1228\t\n  1229\t   The mapping is session state only: it starts empty on a fresh\n  1230\t   session and is NOT reconstructed across rehydration. A session\n  1231\t   rebuilt over a rehydrated index therefore recovers claim-free for\n  1232\t   its pre-existing programs (the accepted policy); a new admission\n  1233\t   is never assigned to an old, unmapped program.\"\n  1234\t  [state]\n  1235\t  (:call-site-admissions state))\n  1236\t\n  1237\t\n  1238\t(defn- indexed-program-roots\n  1239\t  \"The `[metadata-entity root]` of every program the indexer has\n  1240\t   published: `[]` when nothing is published yet, or nil when the\n  1241\t   published index cannot be read.\"\n  1242\t  [indexer]\n  1243\t  (if-not (:manifest-address indexer)\n  1244\t    []\n  1245\t    (try\n  1246\t      (into []\n  1247\t            (comp (filter (fn [[_e a _v _t _m]] (= :yin.repl/root a)))\n  1248\t                  (map (fn [[e _a v _t _m]] [e v])))\n  1249\t            (space-index/read-datoms (:content-store indexer)\n  1250\t                                     (:manifest-address indexer)))\n  1251\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _\n  1252\t        nil))))\n  1253\t\n  1254\t\n  1255\t(defn- index-round-succeeded?\n  1256\t  \"True when the index round from indexer `before` to `after` actually\n  1257\t   committed and published: no recorded failure, not lost, a readable\n  1258\t   manifest covering every committed transaction, and at least one\n  1259\t   new transaction. A failed commit or publication preserves the\n  1260\t   prior manifest (`yin.repl.index`), so it proves nothing.\"\n  1261\t  [before after]\n  1262\t  (and (map? before) (map? after)\n  1263\t       (nil? (:failure after))\n  1264\t       (not (:lost? after))\n  1265\t       (some? (:manifest-address after))\n  1266\t       (= (:published after) (:transactions after))\n  1267\t       (> (:transactions after) (:transactions before))))\n  1268\t\n  1269\t\n  1270\t(defn- record-call-site-admissions\n  1271\t  \"Pair each table entry the expander retained since `tables-before`\n  1272\t   with the indexed program this round committed under the same root,\n  1273\t   recording `{metadata-entity full-admission-origin}` on `state`.\n  1274\t\n  1275\t   Pairing is from COMMIT EVIDENCE, never from searching the published\n  1276\t   index: `eval-program` captures the round's\n  1277\t   `:call-site-commit-evidence` (`{:programs-before [...]}` — the\n  1278\t   published programs before indexing — and `:indexer-before`)\n  1279\t   before the index stage runs, and this step consumes and drops it.\n  1280\t   Only programs absent before the round (the entities its successful\n  1281\t   commit actually committed), only after the round is verified to\n  1282\t   have committed and published (`index-round-succeeded?`), and only\n  1283\t   when the pairing is unique ON BOTH SIDES for a root — one new\n  1284\t   admission and one newly committed candidate — is a pair recorded.\n  1285\t   Multiple admissions or multiple candidates for one root refuse all\n  1286\t   of them. Pre-existing entities, including rehydrated programs, are\n  1287\t   excluded by construction. Absent evidence records nothing\n  1288\t   (fail-closed), never inferred from counters.\"\n  1289\t  [tables-before state]\n  1290\t  (let [evidence (:call-site-commit-evidence state)\n  1291\t        state (dissoc state :call-site-commit-evidence)\n  1292\t        new-entries (into {}\n  1293\t                          (remove (fn [[k _]]\n  1294\t                                    (contains? tables-before k)))\n  1295\t                          (or (call-site-tables state) {}))\n  1296\t        programs-before (:programs-before evidence)\n  1297\t        programs-after (when (some? evidence)\n  1298\t                         (indexed-program-roots (:indexer state)))]\n  1299\t    (if (or (empty? new-entries)\n  1300\t            (nil? evidence)\n  1301\t            (nil? programs-before)\n  1302\t            (nil? programs-after)\n  1303\t            (not (index-round-succeeded? (:indexer-before evidence)\n  1304\t                                         (:indexer state))))\n  1305\t      state\n  1306\t      (let [before-ms (into #{} (map first) programs-before)\n  1307\t            committed (filterv #(not (contains? before-ms (first %)))\n  1308\t                               programs-after)\n  1309\t            entries-by-root (group-by (fn [[k _]] (second k)) new-entries)\n  1310\t            committed-by-root (group-by second committed)]\n  1311\t        (reduce (fn [st root]\n  1312\t                  (let [entries (get entries-by-root root)\n  1313\t                        candidates (get committed-by-root root)]\n  1314\t                    (if (and (= 1 (count entries))\n  1315\t                             (= 1 (count candidates))\n  1316\t                             (not (contains? (:call-site-admissions st)\n  1317\t                                             (ffirst candidates))))\n  1318\t                      (assoc-in st [:call-site-admissions\n  1319\t                                    (ffirst candidates)]\n  1320\t                                (first (ffirst entries)))\n  1321\t                      st)))\n  1322\t                (update state :call-site-admissions #(or % {}))\n  1323\t                (keys entries-by-root))))))\n  1324\t\n  1325\t\n  1326\t(defn- run-expander-stage\n  1327\t  \"Drive the expander over `program-in` and drain its summary.  It expands\n  1328\t   each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n  1329\t   failed expansion forwards nothing, yet its cursor advances (yin.vm.macro.md\n  1330\t   decision 12).  Returns the state with the expander's progress and the\n  1331\t   drained `{:errors :forwarded}` summary.\"\n  1332\t  [state]\n  1333\t  (let [{:keys [observer consumer]}\n  1334\t        (macro/step {:observer (:observer state), :consumer (:expander state)})\n  1335\t        [expander summary] (macro/drain-errors consumer)]\n  1336\t    [(assoc state :observer observer :expander expander) summary]))\n  1337\t\n  1338\t\n  1339\t(defn- run-evaluator-stage\n  1340\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n  1750\t\n  1751\t\n  1752\t(defn- eval-program\n  1753\t  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n  1754\t   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n  1755\t   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n  1756\t   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n  1757\t   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the code and AST indexers and then\n  1758\t   the evaluator only when a program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n  1759\t   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n  1760\t   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n  1761\t   is appended.\n  1762\t\n  1763\t   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n  1764\t   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n  1765\t   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n  1766\t   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n  1767\t   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n  1768\t\n  1769\t   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n  1770\t   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n  1771\t   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n  1772\t  [state program]\n  1773\t  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n  1774\t    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1775\t    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n  1776\t          tables-before (call-site-tables state')\n  1777\t          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n  1778\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n  1779\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n  1780\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n  1781\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n  1782\t        (let [expanded (try\n  1783\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n  1784\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1785\t                                   :clj Exception\n  1786\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n  1787\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n  1788\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n  1789\t            failed\n  1790\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n  1791\t                  indexed (if (pos? forwarded)\n  1792\t                            ;; commit evidence is captured BEFORE the\n  1793\t                            ;; index stage runs: the published programs\n  1794\t                            ;; and indexer as they stood, so the recorder\n  1795\t                            ;; pairs only what this round commits\n  1796\t                            (let [evidence\n  1797\t                                  {:programs-before\n  1798\t                                   (indexed-program-roots (:indexer expanded))\n  1799\t                                   :indexer-before (:indexer expanded)}]\n  1800\t                              (-> expanded\n  1801\t                                  run-index-stage\n  1802\t                                  run-ast-index-stage\n  1803\t                                  (assoc :call-site-commit-evidence evidence)\n  1804\t                                  ((fn [s]\n  1805\t                                     (record-call-site-admissions\n  1806\t                                       tables-before s)))))\n  1807\t                            expanded)]\n  1808\t              (with-index-notice\n  1809\t                (cond\n  1810\t                  (> (ingress-gaps indexed) (ingress-gaps state'))\n  1811\t                  [(assoc indexed :ingress-loss? true)\n  1812\t                   (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n  1813\t\n  1814\t                  (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state indexed)\n  1815\t\n  1816\t                  :else [(assoc indexed :vm (:vm state))\n  1817\t                         (format-expansion-errors errors)])\n  1818\t                (when (pos? forwarded)\n  1819\t                  [(index/notice (:indexer expanded) (:indexer indexed))\n  1820\t                   (ast-index/notice (:ast-indexer indexed))])))))))))\n  1821\t\n  1822\t\n  1823\t(defn- installed-text\n  1824\t  \"The languages and ids `catalog` holds, for a refused selection to name:\n  1825\t   a name that is neither is a typo, not a missing frontend.\"\n  1826\t  [catalog]\n  1827\t  (let [entries (:yang.frontend/entries catalog)\n  1828\t        listed (fn [xs] (str/join \" \" (map pr-str (sort (distinct xs)))))]\n  1829\t    (str \"installed: \"\n  1830\t         (listed (map (comp :yang.frontend/language :manifest) (vals entries)))\n  1831\t         \" (ids \" (listed (map first (keys entries))) \")\")))\n  1832\t\n  1833\t\n  1834\t(defn- select-frontend\n  1835\t  \"Select the frontend `lang` names in `catalog`: a qualified id selects\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
