:stream observer)))\n  1163\t                   carried\n  1164\t                   observer))\n  1165\t        drained (assoc state\n  1166\t                       :observer (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n  1167\t                       :row-observer (drain-observer\n  1168\t                                       (resume (:row-observer state)))\n  1169\t                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state))\n  1170\t                       :ast-indexer (ast-index/skip (:ast-indexer state)))\n  1171\t        [state' output-text]\n  1172\t        (drain-output\n  1173\t          (cond-> drained\n  1174\t            (> (ingress-gaps drained) (ingress-gaps state))\n  1175\t            (assoc :ingress-loss? true)))]\n  1176\t    [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))\n  1177\t\n  1178\t\n  1179\t(defn- run-index-stage\n  1180\t  \"Drive the code indexer's observer over `program-out`: it commits each\n  1181\t   forwarded packet as one transaction and publishes the covered indexes.\n  1182\t   It runs before the evaluator, so a program is indexed whether its VM\n  1183\t   returns, parks, or raises; the two observers meet only at the medium.\"\n  1184\t  [state]\n  1185\t  (update state :indexer index/step (:round state)))\n  1186\t\n  1187\t\n  1188\t(defn- run-ast-index-stage\n  1189\t  \"Drive the AST indexer's observer over `program-out`: it adds each\n  1190\t   forwarded packet's rows and occurrences to the session's `$ast` and\n  1191\t   `$occ` relations.  It runs before the evaluator for the same reason the\n  1192\t   code indexer does, and neither indexer reads the other.\"\n  1193\t  [state]\n  1194\t  (update state :ast-indexer ast-index/step))\n  1195\t\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1836:(defn ready?\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc:217:(defn run-on-stream\n   155\t\n   156\t   Returns `{:status :ok :batch batch :observer observer'}` on `ok`, where the\n   157\t   successor state carries the exact returned cursor; `{:status :bl